{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>See.</b> And the sage who has no inheritance or silver shall rejoice in his wisdom and not be angered on account of his poverty, for it has already been decreed upon him what was decreed from the six days of Genesis, and those who understand the work of the heavens will understand — and this is the meaning of \"which Elohim made,\" that Elohim set in place in all His work a force over the first form, and anyone whose disposition is warped in a matter of money or anything else has no remedy."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "The phrase מביני מלאכת השמים יבינו is translated hyper-literally; the syntax is compressed and possibly elliptical."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:28:07.131046493Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}